## 18. Negative Wrap-Around

Example:

```text
A - 1 = Z
B - 2 = Z
C - 4 = Y
```

The alphabet is circular.

---

## 19. Letter-to-Number Coding

Letters can first be converted into numbers.

Example:

```text
CAT
```

Positions:

```text
C = 3
A = 1
T = 20
```

So:

```text
CAT → 3,1,20
```

Possible further rules:

```text
sum = 3 + 1 + 20 = 24
```

Therefore:

```text
CAT → 24
```

---

## 20. Sum Coding

Example:

```text
DOG
```

Positions:

```text
D = 4
O = 15
G = 7
```

Sum:

```text
4 + 15 + 7 = 26
```

Therefore:

```text
DOG → 26
```

---

## 21. Product Coding

Example:

```text
BAD
```

Positions:

```text
B = 2
A = 1
D = 4
```

Product:

```text
2 × 1 × 4 = 8
```

So:

```text
BAD → 8
```

---

## 22. Difference Coding

Sometimes:

```text
CODE = last position - first position
```

Example:

```text
DOG
```

```text
G = 7
D = 4

7 - 4 = 3
```

Possible code:

```text
3
```

Always determine the exact rule from examples.

---

## 23. Average Coding

Example:

```text
ABC
```

Positions:

```text
1,2,3
```

Average:

```text
(1+2+3)/3 = 2
```

So:

```text
ABC → 2
```

This is less common but possible.

---

## 24. Sum of Odd/Even Positions

For a word:

```text
ABCDE
```

Odd positions:

```text
A,C,E
```

Even positions:

```text
B,D
```

Possible code:

```text
Odd sum = 1+3+5 = 9
Even sum = 2+4 = 6
```

Therefore:

```text
ABCDE → 9,6
```

---

## 25. Vowel-Consonant Coding

A question may classify:

```text
Vowels = A,E,I,O,U
Consonants = remaining letters
```

Example:

```text
APPLE
```

Vowels:

```text
A,E
```

Consonants:

```text
P,P,L
```

A code may be:

```text
2 vowels, 3 consonants
```

---

## 26. Letter Type Coding

A rule may depend on:

```text
Vowel
Consonant
Prime-position letter
Composite-position letter
Odd-position letter
Even-position letter
```

Example:

```text
A = odd position
B = even position
```

Then:

```text
CAT
```

positions:

```text
3,1,20
```

classification:

```text
odd, odd, even
```

---
